    "body": "Problem:\n`:jumps` and `getjumplist()` both call `cleanup_jumplist()`, which deletes the tail entry when it points at the cursor line. Merely querying the jumplist therefore destroys it, e.g. `autocmd CursorMoved * call getjumplist()` erases entries as the cursor passes over them.\n\nSolution:\nDo the \"useless/phantom jump\" removal (#9805) only when the entry is used, in `get_jumplist()` (`<C-O>`/`<C-I>`). `:jumps` hides that entry instead of deleting it, so its output is unchanged; `getjumplist()` reports the list as it is (matching Vim, so the Nvim-specific expectation in `test_jumplist.vim` is reverted to Vim's).\n\nFixes #33598\n\nTests (local, Linux, RelWithDebInfo):\n- `test/functional/editor/jump_spec.lua`: 19 passed; the new test fails with the old `mark.c`.\n- `test/old/testdir/test_jumplist.vim`: 4 passed.\n- `test/functional/shada`: 290 passed.\n- `make lintc`: clean.\n\nAI assistance disclosure: prepared with AI assistance and reviewed before submitting; the commit carries an `AI-assisted` trailer.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-12T13:55:51Z",
